From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DmaBufSeek <dmabuf@local>
Date: Tue, 25 Nov 2026 09:40:00
Subject: [PATCH 0007] dma-buf: set FMODE_LSEEK so vfs_llseek reaches llseek

0006 wired .llseek = dma_buf_llseek in dma_buf_fops and the function is in
kallsyms, but on the device every lseek() on an exported dma-buf fd still
returned ESPIPE, including SEEK_SET:

    SEEK_SET: -1 errno=29 (ESPIPE)
    SEEK_END: -1 errno=29 (ESPIPE)

Cause: dma_buf fds are created with anon_inode_getfile(), which allocates the
file through alloc_file(&path, OPEN_FMODE(flags), fops) and therefore does not
set FMODE_LSEEK (only do_dentry_open() does).  fs/read_write.c vfs_llseek():
"fn = no_llseek; if (file->f_mode & FMODE_LSEEK) { if (file->f_op->llseek)
fn = file->f_op->llseek; }" -- so the fops slot was never consulted and
no_llseek() returned ESPIPE for every whence.

Set FMODE_LSEEK on the dma-buf file in dma_buf_export_named() (after the
anon_inode_getfile() error check, which the 3.10 code also lacked).  SEEK_END
then returns dmabuf->size through dma_buf_llseek().

---
--- a/drivers/base/dma-buf.c	2026-11-25 09:24:22.056744115 -0500
+++ b/drivers/base/dma-buf.c	2026-11-25 09:24:22.149500497 -0500
@@ -182,6 +182,16 @@
 	dmabuf->exp_name = exp_name;
 
 	file = anon_inode_getfile("dmabuf", &dma_buf_fops, dmabuf, flags);
+	if (IS_ERR(file)) {
+		kfree(dmabuf);
+		return ERR_CAST(file);
+	}
+	/* anon_inode_getfile() allocates the file through alloc_file() and so
+	 * does not set FMODE_LSEEK (only do_dentry_open() does).  vfs_llseek()
+	 * gates on that bit before calling f_op->llseek, so without this every
+	 * lseek() on a dma-buf fd returns ESPIPE even though
+	 * dma_buf_fops.llseek is wired. */
+	file->f_mode |= FMODE_LSEEK;
 
 	dmabuf->file = file;
 
